  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 1014 PM MDT Sat Oct 3 2026\n\nThrough the early week, rain chances remain near zero as an upper \nhigh sits near the Four Corners. Moisture remains south of the \nborder, creeping northward to about the I-10 corridor Mon/Tue as the \nupper high weakens with PWs rising to around 0.9\". At the surface, a \nridge of high pressure extends from the Plains. The pressure \ngradient will be most pronounced on Sun, resulting in breezy E winds \nthrough the day, especially along and W of the Divide. Gusts to 30 \nmph are forecast along the I-10 corridor, closer to 40 mph for \nHidalgo and southern Grant Counties. Winds are expected to remain \nbelow advisory criteria out west. \n\nBreeziness lingers out west for Mon with lighter winds elsewhere as \nthe gradient loosens. Troughing aloft and at the surface develops \nthrough midweek across northern MX and south Texas as moisture \nlevels decline, leaving us with minimal rain chances. Seasonably \ncool temperatures through Mon, then warming up slightly for the \nrest of the week to near average. Winds will be generally light \nfor mid-late week with breeziness returning out west Thu-Sat.",
